# Source for the Front's constitutional and press campaign: Fakhreddin Azimi,
# Iran: The Crisis of Democracy, 1941–1953, ch. 5, pp. 250–267.
# The recurring defense work and its effects are counterfactual.
title: Legal Defense and Repression Response
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: public_campaign
view-if: legal_defense_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; legal_defense_timer = 5

= Legal Defense and Repression Response

Restrictions do not affect every component in the same way. The secretariat
can concentrate scarce money on particular legal cases or assemble a public
record that makes separate incidents legible as a constitutional problem.

One route gives immediate assistance; the other creates information and public
pressure. Neither guarantees relief from the authorities.

- @defense_cases
- @defense_test_case
- @defense_record

@defense_cases
title: Fund individual legal cases
subtitle: The <span class="term term-national-front">Front</span> stands behind named defendants and pays the cost of keeping their cases alive
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; constitutional_legitimacy += 4; organizational_reach += 2; toilers_relation += 2

The secretariat selects defensible cases, pays for counsel and filings, and
keeps affected organizers connected to their committees.
{!<span class="term term-social-democratic">!}Toilers' Party{!</span>!}
organizers see that the
coalition will spend common resources on members under pressure.

The legal work reinforces the
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front's{!</span>!} constitutional
claim and preserves some
organizational continuity. The broader pattern of restrictions remains only
partly documented.

- @post_event: Continue

@defense_test_case
title: Carry a test case through every available proceeding
subtitle: A sustained lawsuit creates a record that later defendants and petitioners can reuse
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Requires 2 resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; constitutional_legitimacy += 5; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 4; organizational_reach += 2

Counsel selects a case with a clear procedural record and pays the costs of
filings, appearances, copied documents, and continued contact with the
defendant's organization. The campaign refuses to promise a favorable court.

Even an adverse decision now leaves a record other lawyers can cite and
organizers can explain. The treasury bears the full cost of seeing the case
through.

- @post_event: Continue

@defense_record
title: Publish a common record of restrictions
subtitle: A printed catalogue makes repression public—and turns every accusation toward the <span class="term term-royalist">Court</span>
on-arrival: press_capacity += 5; public_mandate += 3; shah_relation -= 1

Editors and local committees compile dates, orders, interrupted meetings, and
other reports into one careful dossier. Claims that cannot be checked are
marked as uncertain rather than repeated as fact.

The record gives the press and leadership a clearer picture and widens public
attention. Its direct attribution of responsibility further strains relations
with the {!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Court{!</span>!}.

- @post_event: Continue
